Yumora User Agreement and Privacy Policy
Last Updated: 2026.10.12
Operator: Yumora
Contact Email: Mukantghadi@icloud.com
Yumora provides features including food information recording, photo adding, dining check-ins, ratings, expense records, food culture records, and data statistics, along with account, chat, and audio/video call services.
The specific features are subject to the app version you use and the content actually made available. Expense records and statistics are for personal life records only and do not constitute payment, settlement, or financial proof.
Part 1: User Agreement
1. Account Use
You should provide registration information as required on the page, keep your account and login credentials secure, and must not impersonate others or use another person's account without authorization.
If you discover your account has been stolen or there is any abnormality, please contact us promptly. We will assist after reasonable identity verification.
To delete your account, please submit a request via [Profile -> Delete account], or contact us at [Mukantghadi@icloud.com] for assistance. The rules for processing information related to account deletion are described in the Privacy Policy.
2. User Content and Conduct
You should ensure that you have lawful rights or necessary authorization for any photos, text, voice, video, or other content you upload or send, and must not infringe on others' privacy, portrait rights, copyright, or other lawful rights.
You must not use this service for fraud, harassment, spreading illegal information, malicious attacks on the system, or other illegal or non-compliant activities.
You retain the rights you lawfully hold over your original content. To enable functions you voluntarily choose, such as storage, display, and sending, you permit us to process such content to the extent necessary to provide the relevant services; this permission does not include using the content for unrelated commercial promotion.
Where others' information is involved, please obtain necessary authorization. Before sending content to other users, please confirm the recipients and the scope of the content.
Part 2: Privacy Policy
1. Information We Process and Purposes
We process information within the scope necessary to achieve the corresponding purposes based on the features you use.
 
Scenario	Information Involved	Purpose
Registration and login	Username, password, account identifier, login status	Create account, verify identity, maintain login
Profile	Nickname and avatar you set	Display profile, identify communication counterparts
Food and culture records	Text, photos, categories, etc. you enter	Display and manage records
Dining check-ins and statistics	Restaurant name, rating, expense amount, time, comments, and photos	Generate check-in records and statistics
Notifications and service operation	Push identifier, device and system version, app version, IP address, and necessary operation logs	Send notifications, establish network connections, troubleshoot
2. System Permissions
We request relevant permissions based on the features you voluntarily use.
Camera: To take photos of food, check-ins, culture records, and avatars, as well as for video calls.
Microphone: To record and send voice messages.
Photo library read or image selection: To select photos and videos you wish to add or send. When using the system image picker, the app receives only the content you voluntarily select.
Photo library write: To save selected images and group QR codes to your photo library.
Notifications: To remind you of messages, incoming calls, or related service notifications.
You can manage permissions in your device's system settings. Denying or withdrawing a permission will affect features that depend on it, but should not affect other features that do not require that permission.
3. Information Security
We will take security measures appropriate to the risks of information processing, restrict unauthorized access, and impose necessary protection requirements on relevant service providers.
In the event of a personal information security incident, we will take remedial measures in accordance with the law and fulfill notification and reporting obligations as required.
4. Policy Updates
If this policy undergoes important changes, we will notify you via in-app notifications or other means. For changes that require renewed consent under the law, we will carry out the relevant processing after obtaining such consent.
